  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 7.5. Increased capacity of constituents to develop fair and effective labour migration frameworks, institutions and services to protect migrant workers</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2020, the Ministry of Labour and Social Welfare (MoLSW) together with social partners developed and published pocketbook designed to deliver most recent useful information for migrant workers. 7,890 copies were distributed to quarantine centres across Lao PDR and to Migrant Resource Centres (MRCs) through the Department of Labour and Social Welfare at the provincial level. 
The MolSW strengthened coordination with other stakeholders through Migration Networking Group meetings. These networking meetings provided an opportunity for partners and stakeholders to exchange experiences and lessons learned on supporting migrant workers in the country, to ensure initiatives build synergies and to ensure that there are consultative dialogues among key stakeholders and ministries on labour migration, including on ending violence and harassment. 
In July 2021, the Lao Federation of Trade Union (LFTU) in Bokeo province launched a new Migrant Resource Centre. Through the new Bokeo MRC as well as the existing Savannakhet MRC, the LFTU expanded its strategies to provide specific services for women migrant workers and to integrate  issues of gender equality, women&apos;s empowerment, violence, harassment and trafficking in persons. Over 3,800 potential and returnee migrant workers, their families and service providers have benefited from the Migrant Resource Centres&apos; services. LFTU outreach to factories reached (2,553) workers (2,144 women) with information about formal migration channels and processes, and increased their understanding of labour exploitation, violence and harassment at work, and trafficking in persons. With support of the Government of Australia and Canada and the European Union, the ILO provided a series of capacity development trainings and workshops on migration to national and local stakeholders. Through facilitation of the ILO with the authorities in Lao PDR and Thailand, ILO contributed to the development and revision of a Pocket book.
The ILO, with assistance of the European Union, supported Ministry of Labour and Social Welfare to facilitate dialogues that strengthen multi stakeholder knowledge and experience sharing, coordination and collaboration. The ILO has also provided technical inputs to shape these dialogues, and mainstream the issues faced by women migrant workers into dialogues and capacity building activities, as well as raise awareness of duty bearers and service providers. 
With support of the Government of Australia and Canada and the European Union, capacity development and technical support have been provided in support of  the established Migrant Resource Centres (MRCs)in Lao PDR, which also enabled the MRC staff to conduct outreach activities to communities and expand services to women migrant workers . 
The ILO also built capacity of the MoLSW, LFTU and the National Statistics Office on the issue of violence and harassment in the world of work - including ILO Convention No. 190, and  sex-disaggregated labour migration statistics.</narrative>
   </description>
